      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "My apologies for the confusion. Let's get back on track with a professional approach to your Master Service Agreement (MSA) for your raw material supplier. Here's a revised checklist of standard terms and conditions you should consider including in your MSA to protect your interests:\n\n1. **Price Adjustment Mechanism**: Clearly define how and when prices can be adjusted. This should include a formula or index that ties price changes to market fluctuations, ensuring that price hikes are justified and predictable.\n\n2. **Minimum and Maximum Supply Quantities**: Specify the minimum and maximum quantities of raw materials that will be supplied to you. This helps manage your inventory levels and ensures a steady supply without overstocking.\n\n3. **Force Majeure Clause**: Include a force majeure clause that covers unforeseen events (e.g., natural disasters, political instability, pandemics) that could disrupt the supply chain. This clause should outline the obligations of both parties in such events.\n\n4. **Termination Clause**: Clearly state the conditions under which either party can terminate the agreement. This should include notice periods, penalties for early termination, and any obligations to continue supplying materials until the termination date.\n\n5. **Dispute Resolution**: Outline the process for resolving disputes, whether through",
